@*
    Styling for a drawing shown inside a post or a message. It fills the card's width and keeps the shape it was
    drawn in, which the viewBox does on its own — there is nothing here that has to know the board's size.
*@
<style>
    /* The ground is the page's deepest tone rather than a glass tint, because a sent message's bubble is painted
       in the theme's own primary and a translucent ground would let that colour through — leaving a drawing in
       primary ink almost invisible on it. */
    .drawing-view {
        display: block;
        width: @(AppMeasures.Percent.Full)%;
        height: auto;
        border-radius: @(AppMeasures.Radius.Large)px;
        background: @(AppColors.BackgroundDeep.ToRgbaHex(true));
    }
</style>
